+# Handoff Snapshot — Iteration 1
+
+## Goal
+
+Find and fix the metrics bug where `total_output_tokens` is inflated when KV cache preemption occurs.
+
+## Key Discoveries
+
+- **Root cause confirmed**: `sim/simulator.go:647` increments `TotalOutputTokens++` in the decode loop of `executeBatchStep`. When a request is preempted, `batch_formation.go:232` resets `ProgressIndex` to 0, causing the request to re-enter prefill and decode from scratch. Each re-generated output token is counted again.
+- **Magnitude**: Before fix, small KV (600 blocks, 265 preemptions) reports 114,630 output tokens vs large KV (5000 blocks, 88 preemptions) 106,083 — a delta of 8,547 phantom tokens. Even the "large KV" run had 1,001 phantom tokens from its 88 preemptions.
+- **Fix**: Move `TotalOutputTokens` accumulation to `recordRequestCompletion`, computing from `ProgressIndex - len(InputTokens)` at completion time. This value is correct regardless of preemption history.
+- **After fix**: Both runs report 105,082 tokens — identical, as expected for the same workload.
+- **Existing convention preserved**: The system counts N-1 output tokens for an N-output-token request (first token counted as TTFT, not as an output token). This convention is unchanged.
+
+## System Interface
+
+- **Build:** `go build -o blis main.go`
+- **Run baseline:** `./blis run --model qwen/qwen3-14b --rate 20 --num-requests 200 --seed 42 --total-kv-blocks 5000`
+- **Output format:** JSON to stdout under `=== Simulation Metrics ===`
+- **Baseline result:** `total_output_tokens: 105082` (post-fix)
+
+## Code Map
+
+- `sim/simulator.go:647` — Former location of `TotalOutputTokens++` in decode loop (removed)
+- `sim/simulator.go:490-494` — New location of `TotalOutputTokens` accumulation in `recordRequestCompletion`
+- `sim/batch_formation.go:232` — `preemptedRequest.ProgressIndex = 0` (the reset that causes double-counting)
+- `sim/simulator.go:635-660` — `executeBatchStep` decode loop (ITL still appended here, unchanged)
+- `sim/simulator_test.go:2073-2076` — Existing test with expected value 49 (verifies convention)
+
+## Code Targets
+
+- `sim/simulator.go:647`: Remove `sim.Metrics.TotalOutputTokens++` from decode loop
+- `sim/simulator.go:490`: Add `TotalOutputTokens += ProgressIndex - len(InputTokens)` in `recordRequestCompletion`
+
+## What I Tried That Didn't Work
+
+- Initially considered tracking per-request `OutputTokensCounted` field — overly complex for this bug
+- Considered using `len(req.OutputTokens)` at completion — wrong for length-capped requests
+- Considered using `len(req.ITL)` — would be wrong for preempted requests (ITL also not reset on preemption)
+
+## What I Excluded and Why
+
+- **ITL double-counting on preemption**: `req.ITL` is also appended during decode and NOT reset on preemption, so ITL-derived E2E metrics may also be affected. This is a separate issue — the current fix only addresses `TotalOutputTokens`.
+- **TTFT/FirstTokenTime on preemption**: Neither `TTFTSet` nor `FirstTokenTime` are reset on preemption. A preempted request that re-enters prefill would re-record TTFT if `TTFTSet` check fails. This is also separate.
+
+## Evolution of Thinking
+
+Initially focused on where `TotalOutputTokens` is incremented. The key insight was that `ProgressIndex` gets fully reset to 0 on preemption (not partially — it goes back to beginning of prefill), meaning every decode token is re-counted. The fix was simple once I understood that `ProgressIndex` at completion time is always correct regardless of preemption history, making it the right basis for counting.
+
+## Current Status
+
+- **Validated:** Fix produces identical `total_output_tokens` for small and large KV caches. All existing tests pass (sim, cluster, golden dataset). Regression test added.
+- **Uncertain:** Whether ITL/TTFT metrics are also affected by the same preemption-reset issue (likely yes, but separate bugs).
+- **Suggested next:** Investigate ITL and TTFT metrics for similar double-counting on preemption.
+
+## Warnings & Constraints
+
+- The existing `TotalOutputTokens` convention counts N-1 tokens per N-output-token request (the "first token" is TTFT, not counted as output). The fix preserves this. If this convention is ever questioned, the tests at lines 2073-2076 and 1599-1600 document it explicitly.
+- The `cmd/` test suite has a pre-existing network listener failure (`hfconfig_test.go:269`) unrelated to this change.
